    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d527">

                <pb facs="0697" n="573" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg573"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2009: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Harbin</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-03-24T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 24,
                                1921—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>For Johnson from Stevens.</p>
                <p>“Your cable March 14th, 7 p.m.<anchor n="89" xml:id="d527-f1"/> Technical Board
                    must maintain firm stand on all its rights regardless of results. Efforts to
                    have amended Allied agreement giving enlarged complete powers being pushed by
                    Department. You must hold the situation despite intrigues.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
